{
  "kanji": "婦",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 婦\ntitle: woman; wife\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 11\nradical: 女\nradicalNumber: 38\nonyomi: [フ]\nkunyomi: [よめ]\ndistractors: [帰, 始, 姉]\n---\n\n# 婦 — woman; wife\n\n**Strokes:** 11 · **Key (radical):** 女 (no. 38) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n婦 carries woman or wife meanings in compounds. In [夫婦](../words/夫婦.md) (ふうふ), it is the wife member of a married pair.\n主婦 (しゅふ) instead names a housewife or homemaker; the whole word supplies that role.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** use [帰](帰.md) as a visual frame, then deliberately give 婦 the full 女 on the left.\nThis shape comparison is a memory aid, not an origin story.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| フ | on | [夫婦](../words/夫婦.md) (ふうふ) — married couple; 主婦 (しゅふ) — housewife |\n\nThe source also records よめ; the table concentrates on the compound reading フ.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [夫婦](../words/夫婦.md) (ふうふ) — married couple\n- 主婦 (しゅふ) — housewife; homemaker\n- 婦人 (ふじん) — woman; lady; the cited dictionary marks this term as dated and potentially sensitive\n\n## Notes\n\nDo not treat every word containing 婦 as a claim that the woman is married. 婦人 has an adult-woman sense.\nFor [帰](帰.md), inspect the left side; for [始](始.md) and [姉](姉.md), inspect the right side.\n[女](女.md) and [妻](妻.md) share the woman and wife meanings found in 婦; learn which sense a whole word uses.\n\nSources: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project); [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1583640, 1326160, 1496670.\n",
